{"amendments":[{"body":"Fix `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:218-239`: `route_consumed_food` now books the full respiration fraction into DIC/TAN and only then clamps `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` at zero. Under low-DO conditions this creates respired C/N fluxes that were never actually oxidized and undercounts the reserve that should retain the unrespired share. Respiration needs to be scaled by available O2 before routing DIC/TAN and retained reserve.","rationale":"This breaks the shrimp loop under hypoxia and reintroduces a mass/stoichiometry error in exactly the case the old oxygen-limited regression covered."},{"body":"Fix `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:78-86` together with `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:242-245`: `step_daily_shrimp` now refreshes carbonate state only after `update_condition`, but `update_condition` computes NH3 toxicity from `state.water.ph`. Feeding changes TAN/DIC first, so condition, molt stress, and reproduction are all being evaluated from stale pre-feeding pH for the whole day. Recompute carbonate state immediately after `shrimp_feeding` and before the condition-dependent steps.","rationale":"The current ordering delays same-day ammonia/pH effects from feeding and changes shrimp behavior relative to the intended chemistry loop."},{"body":"Revert the fallback added in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:631-670` as used by hatching at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:446-449` and maturation at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:534-536`. `fund_live_shrimp_biomass` now creates new shrimp biomass directly out of DOC/DIC/DON/TAN whenever `reserve_g` is short. That bypasses the explicit reserve pathway this bead introduced, lets juveniles hatch or mature with zero assimilated reserve, and gives shrimp an implausible ability to turn dissolved inorganic pools into tissue.","rationale":"This materially changes population dynamics and breaks the contract that future shrimp realism should build on the reserve pathway rather than bypass it."},{"body":"Fix `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:402-407`: `RemoveShrimp` now computes the exported reserve fraction against `adults_count` only. If all adults are removed while juveniles remain, `removed_frac` becomes 1.0 and the entire shared reserve pool is deleted. The reserve export needs to stay proportional to the whole shrimp population, or another explicit biomass share, not just adults.","rationale":"Current behavior strips remaining juveniles of their reserve whenever the adult cohort is removed."},{"body":"Restore legacy stability-tracker reseeding in `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:179-184` and `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:350-361`. The loader no longer has access to `file_version`, so schema-v2 saves that serialized `StabilityTracker::default()` are treated as valid historical baselines instead of being reseeded. Those saves will register a fake instability swing on the first update after load.","rationale":"This regresses save compatibility for older files and reintroduces a bug that the deleted schema-v2 tracker test previously covered."}],"summary":"Reviewed the task checkpoint range `e5b1784^..851866d` and found five correctness regressions: low-oxygen respiration is no longer O2-limited, carbonate refresh now happens too late for condition/NH3 evaluation, hatching and maturation can mint biomass from dissolved pools, shrimp removal can zero juvenile reserve, and legacy schema-v2 saves no longer reseed default stability trackers."}